# GA106 RTX 3060 (10de:2504) --fuserows physical fuse-row capture, 2026-11-22
# ssdiag 0.8.7, guard-fixed build (CRC_STATUS 0x4555 accepted - the pre-fix
# binary would have aborted; version banner not captured in the paste, the
# guard behavior fingerprints the fixed build). First consumer-die physical
# row capture in the project. IFF_RECORD 0x023f021e: START=542, LAST=575
# (576 rows) - matches the reading-notes 6m table; FUSE_ADDR saved/restored
# = 575 == LAST. Two passes match (576 rows), address restored.
# Provenance: user paste (Windows, elevated probe-driver run).
# CLASSIFICATION: UNKNOWN PER-DEVICE FUSE MATERIAL (standing, 2026-11-22).
# Rows 0x2a..0x4e are device-unique random material (byte entropy 89-100% of
# sample max after dedup; no decodable structure; sizes do NOT match any
# known public format incl. HDCP 1.x 280B / HDCP 2.2 RSA blocks, and differ
# per die). Entropy cannot distinguish secret keys from public verification
# material - both are random-looking by design - so the classification stays
# OPEN until an NVIDIA-side decode exists; HDCP was hypothesized but has no
# structural evidence. Anyone providing row dumps is informed of this
# classification in advance; sharing is optional, and these ranges may be
# redacted or withheld without losing analysis value (the fuse-pool records
# are the analysis-relevant part).
